summary:
I mapped the r11 code (the current source, identical to the t1_012 frozen copy) against r6 (t1_008 frozen) and read the last two request/response pairs of all 8 failed runs.

v3 is uc7 plus these layers:
- an extended action contract: 5 new decision types and 11 required output fields;
- persistent shared geometry (GeometryMemory through r9; the policy switched to LocalGeometryMemory in r10);
- adaptive fragment/motion primitives that check the sweep and every emitted command;
- semantic programs (up to 24 stages; compact pick_place operations from r8; local recovery from r7);
- a visual watch, a two-view interaction monitor, an operation runtime (r7) and local stereo perception (r7);
- a 180 s bounded transport, and wire-only history projection (r10).

Main findings:
- **One exit funnel.** All 8 failures ended as EvidenceAcquisitionFailed through the same path: a geometry or evidence gate paused execution, the model was called, and the view planner offered 0 candidates. The model then escalated in 6 runs. In 2 runs (r10 t1_011, r11 t1_012) it chose acquire_evidence even though the request already advertised 0 candidates, which is a terminal stop by construction (agent_speedup_v3.py:300-302).
- **Root gates.** Strict sweep coverage appears in 6 of the 8 chains, strict overlap in 4, payload/attachment uncertainty in 2. Tracking mismatch ended t1_011. In t1_012, a neighbour (milk) went stale after a predicted contact, which broke lift-goal derivation and disabled view planning.
- **Gates drive the model calls, even in the success.** In r6 t1_008, 36 of the 39 follow-up calls came after a gate pause; model time was 83.9% of control time at 33.4 s per call.
- **r10 moved strictness rather than removing it.** Coverage stopped being a veto, but new hard blocking reasons appeared and program-level freshness requirements remain.
- **Misleading blocker.** The blocker shown to the model omits tracking, so it can contradict the real pause cause (t1_011).
- **Unused local-evidence paths.** None of the r7 local-evidence paths ever produced an accepted event in r7–r11.
